        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat: add Podman agent sandbox backend",
        "body": "Closes #101348\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nOpenClaw supports Docker-backed agent sandboxing and separately supports running the Gateway under Podman, but Podman-first users do not have a supported local container backend for sandboxed agent tools. They currently need Docker, an unsupported Docker-compatible shim/socket path, or a non-container sandbox backend.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis adds a bundled `podman` sandbox plugin that registers a first-class Podman backend through the existing sandbox backend SDK, while reusing the Docker-compatible sandbox container settings for image, mounts, env, network, capabilities, tmpfs, setup commands, and resource limits. The implementation keeps browser sandboxes and Docker GPU support fail-closed for Podman, preserves Docker-specific user fallback behavior, and maps Podman no-network sandboxes correctly into Codex external sandbox policy.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers can set `agents.defaults.sandbox.backend: \"podman\"` to run agent sandbox commands in rootless Podman containers. Writable workspace mounts work with default rootless Podman through `keep-id`, policy/doctor can observe Podman container posture, and `openclaw sandbox` lifecycle operations can describe and remove Podman runtimes.\n\n## Evidence\n\nFocused tests:\n\n```sh\nOPENCLAW_HEAVY_CHECK_LOCK_SCOPE=worktree node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run extensions/podman/src/config.test.ts extensions/podman/src/podman.test.ts extensions/podman/src/backend.test.ts extensions/policy/src/doctor/register.test.ts src/plugin-sdk/api-baseline.test.ts src/agents/sandbox/context.user-fallback.test.ts extensions/codex/src/app-server/dynamic-tool-build.test.ts\n```\n\nResult: 4 Vitest shards passed.\n\nLive Podman proof with Podman 5.8.3:\n\n- Built `openclaw-sandbox:bookworm-slim` with Podman.\n- Created a real Podman sandbox backend container.\n- Read `/workspace/probe.txt` from the mounted workspace.\n- Wrote `/workspace/out.txt` from inside the sandbox.\n- Verified workdir `/workspace`.\n- Verified configured env propagation.\n- Removed the live smoke container afterward.\n\nObserved live smoke output:\n\n```text\npodman-live-ok|sandbox-write|/workspace|podman\n```\n\nAdditional checks:\n\n```sh\ngit diff --check\n.agents/skills/autoreview/scripts/autoreview --mode local\n```\n\nResult: whitespace check passed, and autoreview reported no accepted/actionable findings.\n\nKnown proof gap: remote Crabbox/Testbox proof was not run because the local Crabbox binary is installed and accepted by the wrapper, but the `blacksmith` CLI is not installed/authenticated on this machine, so `blacksmith-testbox` readiness is blocked before lease warmup.\n",
